<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p>
This Privacy Policy explains how the iOS app <strong>Learnaroo</strong> handles personal data. 
Protecting your privacy is a top priority. The app is designed to process only the data that is technically necessary. 
Learnaroo does not use tracking tools, analytics services, profiling, advertising, or social media plugins.
</p>

<h2>Data Controller</h2>
<p>
<strong>Learnaroo</strong><br />
Email: <a href="mailto:info@learnaroo.app">info@learnaroo.app</a>
</p>

<h2>Principle: No Processing of Personal Data</h2>
<p>Learnaroo does not process any personal data that can identify you. In particular, the app does not process:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Names</li>
  <li>Contact details</li>
  <li>Location data</li>
  <li>User behavior profiles</li>
  <li>Device identifiers</li>
  <li>IP addresses for analytics purposes</li>
  <li>Content you enter into the app</li>
</ul>

<p>No data is transmitted to us or to third parties.</p>

<h2>Processing by Apple</h2>
<p>
When downloading and using the app, Apple (App Store) may process technical data independently. 
We have no influence over this data processing. Apple is solely responsible for it.
</p>

<p>
If you have enabled sharing of diagnostics data in iOS settings, Apple may collect anonymous crash reports. 
We do not receive or access this data.
</p>

<h2>Legal Basis</h2>
<p>
The app is designed in accordance with applicable data protection laws. Since no personal data is processed, 
no specific legal basis is required.
</p>

<p>
The app is not specifically targeted at users in the European Union. As no personal data is processed, 
the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) does not apply.
</p>

<h2>Technical Data Processing (Local on Your Device)</h2>
<p>To provide app functionality, the following data may be stored locally on your device only:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Your app preferences or saved items</li>
  <li>Scheduled times for push notifications (if enabled)</li>
</ul>

<p>
This data never leaves your device. You can disable push notifications at any time in your iOS settings.
</p>

<h2>Data Sources</h2>
<p>
Learnaroo may display information sourced from publicly available resources.
</p>

<h2>Technically Necessary Connection Data</h2>
<p>
When using the app, certain technical data (e.g., IP address) may be transmitted as part of normal network communication. 
Learnaroo does not store or analyze this data.
</p>

<h2>No Data Sharing with Third Parties</h2>
<p>
Learnaroo does not share any data with third parties. The app does not use external analytics, tracking tools, 
advertising services, or social media integrations. The app also does not include in-app purchases.
</p>

<h2>Your Rights</h2>
<p>
Since Learnaroo does not process or store personal data:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>No access requests are applicable</li>
  <li>No correction requests are applicable</li>
  <li>No deletion requests are applicable</li>
  <li>No data portability rights apply</li>
</ul>

<p>
You remain in full control:<br />
You can delete any stored data directly within the app.<br />
You can uninstall the app at any time, which removes all locally stored data.
</p>

<h2>Contact / Communication</h2>
<p>
If you contact us via email or in-app contact form, you voluntarily provide personal data such as your name, 
email address, and message. This data is used solely to respond to your request and is not shared with third parties.
</p>

<p>
The data is stored only as long as necessary to process your request and is deleted afterward. 
No profiling or additional use of the data takes place.
</p>

<h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
<p>
We reserve the right to update this Privacy Policy if necessary, for example, due to new features or legal requirements. 
The latest version will always be available in the App Store and within the app.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, you can contact us at:<br />
<a href="mailto:info@learnaroo.app">info@learnaroo.app</a>
</p>

